                                or
        How I Farmed My Way to the /dev/null Rogue High Score 

WARNING: Long, boring post containing graphic description of black 
pudding farming, not suitable for all readers.

This was my fifth ascension, second Rogue ascension, and my first 
ascension in the /dev/null/net NetHack Tournament. Although this was my 
fifth ascension, this is my first ascension post. I usually start 
composing one, but tend to ramble on too much, and get distracted by 
something, and never finish it. 

I started playing soon after midnight on the first day of the 
tournament, but had a real tough time getting a character to survive. I 
started playing tourists, since that had been my last ascension, but 
wasn't getting anywhere. So for the first ten days I played a succession 
of games as tourists, archeologists, rangers, rogues, archeologists, 
rangers, and rogues again. Finally, after about 35 games, I got a rogue 
that seemed to have some staying power.  

The starting stats were typical for a rogue:

