I don't remember a lot about the early game and my notes never seem to 
contain the info I want. Don't know why I can't figure out how to keep 
useful notes. Anyway, according to my notes, the entrance to the mines 
were on level 3, but the first level was dark, so I skipped them. I got 
telepathy on level 4 and found the first store, a 5 x 6 general store,  
on level 5. I spend a lot of time in the shops naming every item with 
it's base price, and then trying to get my pet to steal anything useful 
I can't afford to buy. I bought some +0 elven mithril. There was a huge 
6 x 10 potion store on level 6. I bought 4 potions of water and noted 
several 300 zm. potions for later acquisition. I also found a magic 
whistle on level 6.

I don't have a good understanding of why I survive long enough to ascend 
in some games but not others, but it's probably the luck of finding a 
few key items early on, at least for me. The magic whistle is always a 
welcome find. The first spellbook I found was Identify, although it was 
hard to use until I could replace the mithril with more spell friendly 
armor and advance divination skill. 

The Oracle was on level 7 and, thus, the entrance to Sokoban on level 8. 
I usually do Sokoban before the mines, so I entered Sokoban. I got 
poison resistance from a Golden Naga Hatchling on the first level of 
Sokoban. Now there's a major memory gap: for some reason, I left Sokoban 
before finishing it and pressed on down.

On lever 9, I found a bones level. I didn't make note of the ghost's 
name thinking I'd find a tombstone. I didn't. The character appeared to 
be a wizard from the makeup of the bones pile: a quarterstaff, a clock, 
some potions, etc. There was also a gray stone that turned out to be a 
luckstone, IIRC. I tamed the cats: Gracie and Bonitia, who were a big 
help later, especially Gracie. Then there was an aligned altar on the 
level with a chest next to it with lots of stuff in it, most of it 
useless, just junk armor and weapons, etc. If the wizard had been 
sacfesting, he wasn't very successful as there were no artifact weapons. 
I guess I hung around for a while sacrificing as I received Sting during 
this period. Doh, should have named it. I also acquired a spellbook of 
detect food along the way and practiced that until I could advance 
divination and cast identify at a reasonable success rate. Still a major 
pain though, as I had to take off my armor to cast spells. My 4 large 
cats served well as bodyguards though. With the stuff already there, I 
decide to make this level my base camp, at least for the time being.

Eventually, I went back and finished Sokoban and got the amulet of 
reflection at turn 16924, according to my notes. There were 2 black 
unicorns in the Sokoban treasure zoo, and I maxed by luck there at turn 
17172, again, according to my notes. So I conclude I must have 
identified some gems back by the altar.

After Sokoban, I proceeded down a few more levels. Since I already had a 
luckstone, I wasn't in a hurry to complete the mines. Level 10 had a 3 x 
11 hardware store, but precious little of interest. I did buy a 
blindfold and a magic marker. Level 11 had a 3 x 8 opulent throne room 
that granted a genocide (master mind flayers, I am deathly afraid of 
those buggers) and see invisible. I also acquired cold resistance on 
this level from a gelatinous cube. I must have fallen thru a trap door 
on this level and fallen all the way to level 14, which turned out to be 
the level with the quest portal. Scurrying back upstairs, on level 13 I 
found a lamp which was different from the oil lamp I had identified by 
price in the level 10 hardware store. So with a magic lamp as a light 
source, I decided to head back up and tackle the mines. I stopped at the 
altar on 9 to check the lamp which turned out to be cursed. At this 
point, Gracie killed and ate a chameleon and became a black dragon. And 
there was much rejoicing.

So it's off to Minetown. I got there at XP 11 and had enough for two 
contributions and got 4 points of AC protection total. The temple was 
lawful. Minesend was the catacombs version and I picked up 4 more 
spellbooks. I finished the mines mainly on the hope of finding a bag of 
holding, but no joy. I'm beginning to have serious weight problems with 
all the daggers, spellbooks, and other crap I'm gathering up. I lug all 
the loot back to base camp, stressed most of the way. I have to ferry 
the stuff up and down stairs in 2 loads. Back at base camp, I learn my 
new spells and decide to convert my magic lamp into a bag of holding. So 
I blessed it up, wished for and got my blessed bag of holding. Finally! 
Unburdened. For a while, at least. So I resumed my downward explorations.

Exploring the rest of level 13, I found another magic lamp. This is 
turning into a nice game. Compensation for some of the crap a had to go 
thru in the first 35 or so games. I mean a tengu with a wand of death. 
Gimme a break. Anyhow, it was very welcome, even if it was cursed. On 
level 16, I got fire resistance from a fire ant. Level 18 was the rogue 
level. On level 19, I offed my first dragon, an orange one, and got 
sleep reisitance. Level 20 had a 5 x 8 opulent throne room, but the 
throne vanished on the first sitting. Level 21 had another opulent 
throne room, 3 x 6 this time, with a black dragon. I manage to take it 
out and got my disintegration resistance. The Sokoban amulet came in 
quite handy. I got a wish from the zoo throne. Since I was playing a 
chaotic, I wasn't going to get Magicbane from sacrificing. I mostly play 
neutrals and have developed a serious addiction to Magicbane. Since 
Sting was the only artifact in the game so far, I decided to wish for 
Magicbane. The tournament was nearly half over and I still hadn't 
ascended so I was getting desperate. I decided to do any thing I could 
to maximize my chance, and I knew Magicbane would be a big help on my 
ascension run, should I survive that long. So I wished for, and got, the 
blessed rustproof +2 Magicbane, which blasted me, but not too badly. 
Clearing the zoo got me XP 13 and I had a potion of Gain Level, so I 
decided to do the quest.

After the abuse from the Master of Thieves, I set off on the quest. I 
found a pair of speed boots on the second quest level. The Master 
Assassin's Lair was on level 6. Apparently, there was nothing of 
interest between 2 and 6, at least it's not in my notes. I took a chance 
on digging down into the Master Assassin's Lair from the level above, 
got lucky and landed in his chamber first try. I had sequestered Gracie, 
the Black Dragon, and Pippin, the last remaining of my 4 large cats, in 
the anteroom, so I could whistle them in. So I did. The Master Assassin 
went down pretty easily and I gathered up the spoils. Alas, poor Pippin 
ate a chameleon corpse and became a spotted jelly. It was with a heavy 
heart that I left him behind. He had been my starting pet and had served 
valiantly and saved my bacon several times in the early game. He would 
be missed. I had a cursed scroll of teleportation, so Gracie and I took 
the express elevator back to Home 1 and reported in the the Master of 
Thieves. Once again, I resisted the urge to kill him. Gonna' have to try 
that one of these days. He sure needs killin'. 

I took all the gold I had gathered up from the leprechauns on the quest 
to Minetown to buy some more protection. Even at XP 14, I had enough for 
11 contributions, and got 7 points of AC, bringing me down to -20. So 
back to level 21 to continue my explorations.

Someplace between 21 and 25, I encountered some more trap doors, and 
wound up on 26. Level 26 had yet another opulent throne room, 3 x 8, and 
I got another genocide which I used for mind flayers. I felt I should be 
close to Medusa by now, so I went on down to check. No notes on level 
27, but Medusa was on level 28 with the center island castle version. 
According to Dylan's Gazetteer, that's the lowest level than Medusa can 
occupy and the Castle must be on the next level. Good to know. I 
retreated to explore the levels I had fallen thru. Level 25 held another 
3 x 8 opulent throne room. This time I got a nasty electric shock and 
felt a strange sensation.

So it's time for a decision. Medusa and the castle are waiting below, 
but I have no means of levitation or water walking. Also, I still 
haven't identified ?ofGenocide. I've never taken on the Castle without 
genociding L. They scare me as much as mind flayers and I don't have any 
experience fighting them. I also like to get rid of the ;'s, but I can 
deal with them on Medusa's level and the Castle (but probably wouldn't 
try Plane of Water before genociding them). How to proceed? I chatted 
with some of the regulars on #nethack and was advised to dig down from 
Medusa's level to the Castle, get the wand, wish up what I needed, and 
go back and whack Medusa. But I was too chicken. That meant a full 
frontal assault on the Castle, not a very rogue-like way to tackle the 
problem. So I decided to retire to a quiet little farm in the country.

I went back to level 9, the only level with any kind of an altar in the 
main dungeon, and homesteaded a farm. By now, my stats look like:

