My notes don't mention it, but judging by my stats, I think Gracie had 
sent the potion shop owner on level 6 off to retirement. I, of course, 
"inherited" his inventory. Using that inventory and some alchemy 
maximized all my stats, except strength.

I used 2 ?'s of earth for raw materials to build a fort around the altar 
and my chest of goodies. I carefully engraved Elbereth 4 times at each 
boulder position using Magicbane to discourage the inevitable giants 
from wrecking my fort. This was finished at turn 41848. Then, with 
Gracie patrolling the level, I dug out every square and proceeded to 
light them via the light spell. Clearing was completed at turn 44629. 
Now it was Gracie's turn to go into retirement. The entrance to Sokoban 
was just one level above, so I took her to the first level of Sokoban 
and we said our goodbyes. A cursed scroll on genocide provided my 
starter herd of black puddings, and I settled down to the restful life 
of a country farmer. I had already been crowned by this time, receiving 
Stormbringer, and had received Frost Brand and a spellbook of 
Invisibilty as gifts. 

My first prayer after sacrificing a batch of puddings yielded only an 
"Attaboy" (You feel that Kos is well-pleased). But 16 turns later, a 
spellbook of Detect Monsters was forthcoming and the goodies began to 
flow. At turn 56959, I stopped sacrificing the puddings and depended 
solely on the death drops from that point on. My AC was -65 and my HP 
were 775 at this point. At turn 58481, I harvested (via a pudding death 
drop) a spellbook of Create Familiar, completing my collection. A magic 
lamp turned up at turn 64986 which was converted into a blessed fixed +2 
helm of brilliance shortly thereafter. Giantslayer was dropped at turn 
68331, but never used. Sometime around turn 68500, I decided I needed to 
add a robe to my outfit. So I paid a visit to my old friend Gracie, who 
was still tame after almost 25000 turns, remarkable loyalty. 

We level 'ported to the VotD, and cleared it out without too much 
trouble. A rogue two weaponing +2 Magicbane and a +7 silver saber is an 
awesome killing machine. When we got over to the west side of the 
valley, Gracie was apparently still peckish and decided to have a Priest 
of Moloch for dessert. I picked up my robe and we went upstairs to get 
the wand. Again, clearing the Castle wasn't much of a problem. For some 
reason, I tamed a silver dragon, instead of slaughtering it for scales. 
Don't know what I was thinking. I got the Castle WoW(0:1) at turn 70442, 
but never used it. It was still in my BoH at 0:1 at ascension. Not that 
I didn't use plenty of other wishes from thrones, magic lamps, and 
smokey potions, which were See Invisible, IIRC. I went upstairs and 
dispatched Medusa and cleared out some of the riff-raff that hangs 
around her castle. Then I took the dragons back to Sokoban. I had 
visions of eventually getting SDSM from the silver one, but based on how 
long Gracie stayed tame, I wasn't sure that would ever happen. In the 
event, it never did and I ascended in the GrayDSM that I think I got 
from a smokey potion wish, but, once again, the notes are silent.

So I returned to the farm and resumed my farming for another 18K to 20K 
turns. My pudding harvests included: a magic marker(0:78), Fire Brand 
(yes, a pudding drop), helm of brilliance, gauntlets of dexterity, an 
ice box, and another magic lamp. My notes don't show what I wished for 
with the magic lamp, but I think I was converting wishes into silver 
daggers during this time period. 

At turn 89224, with the score around 10,000,000, I returned to the VotD 
to explore Gehennom. Juiblex was the first to fall; he went down to two 
weaponed +7 Stormbringer and +7 silver saber in 2 swings. I don't think 
he even landed a blow. Of course, my AC is -87 at this point. Asmodeus, 
Balzebuub, and Orcus all fell to rubber chickens. My usual technique is 
to dig down to the next level whenever I arrive on one of their levels. 
Then I continue my explorations and path clearing until I encounter a 
cockatrice. Then, with the rubber chicken in my BoH, I zip back to the 
upstairs beneath the demon prince, put on my ring of levitation, go up 
the stairs, and whack him with the rubber chicken. Juiblex was on level 
33; Asmodeus, on 34; Baalzebuub, on 37; the stairs to Vlad's, on 38; amd 
Orcus, on 41. All were dispatched except Orcus, where I couldn't find a 
cockatrice that left a corpse. 

As I continued downwards, I encounterd the bottom level of Rodney's 
complex on level 44. I level 'ported to level 54 and wound up on 51, 
where casting Magic Mapping showed no down staircase. I searched out the 
VS and left the Bell of Opening and the Candelabrum with it's 7 candles 
there. I dug out the area around it, lit it, and made a big X with gold 
pieces (X marks the spot). I engraved Elbereth under the Bell and 
Candelabraum and zipped upstairs to continue my mapping. 

I finally got another rubber chicken and paid Orcus a visit. I whacked 
him and cleared out Orcus Town and the maze. Nothing useful showed up in 
the abandoned shops. I busted Orcus' statue and got the wand of death. 
He never had a chance to fire it. I returned to my mapping and clearing. 
Fake wizard tower 2 on level 49 held the portal to Rodney's and I 
entered and cleared the first two levels. Leaving Rodney and the other 
denizens of the third level until later, I finished clearing Gehennom at 
turn 100636. I had dug a path between the up and down stairs on each 
level of Gehennom and a clear path all around the outer edge of each 
level. That way, when the mysterious force drops me someplace, I just 
make a beeline for the edge and I've got a clear path to the stairs. My 
